  "record": {
    "read_status": "full",
    "file_problem": "None; the full paper text is present.",
    "relation": "discusses",
    "tranche": "T6",
    "tranche_reason": "The paper studies test-time sampling and verification for video generation, not held-out pretraining cross-entropy scaling, its extrapolation, or compute-optimal parameter/token allocation. Its inference-time video-quality results are related but do not test any listed claim version.",
    "gate_note": "The paper reports its own results for inference-time candidate sampling in COSMOS video models. Those are not measurements of held-out pretraining loss or the behaviors specified by V1–V7. Table 1 FVD and FID results are recorded as related findings with versions [\"none\"]. The paper also reports other evaluation metrics and results for search algorithms, another modality, and human preference; these do not test a listed version.",
    "test_reason": "The study measures inference-time best-of-N and beam-search gains in COSMOS video quality (FVD, FID, VBench, VideoScore). It does not measure held-out pretraining loss against parameters, tokens or compute. It does not fit power laws, extrapolate, or vary architecture or training allocation. The 4B vs 12B single-pass comparison is two model sizes on generation metrics, with no scaling fit. It does not test any version. Its 'test-time scaling law' is a different construct.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Mostly right. The authors conclude that test-time scaling (best-of-N, and their probabilistic beam search with a fast tokenizer) improves COSMOS video quality in a compute-optimal way, so smaller models can match or beat larger ones at equal inference compute. Note that the 12B single pass still wins on nuScenes FVD in Table 1.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "Uses inference-time best-of-N sampling and verifier-guided search for autoregressive video generation; does not measure the original held-out language-model pretraining-loss scaling method.",
    "method_sensitivity": "Reported video-quality outcomes vary with test-time sample count and search algorithm; the paper also compares verifier/reward choices. These sensitivities concern inference-time video evaluation, not the listed pretraining-loss claims.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "For COSMOS-4B, best-of-N gains are modest. nuScenes FID falls steadily from 67.75 to 45.75 (N=1 to 16). Waymo metrics barely move, and Waymo FVD rebounds at N=16.",
        "proposed_claim": "Inference-time candidate sampling with rule-based verifiers improves video world-model generation quality, with diminishing and dataset-dependent returns.",
        "row_ids": [
          "r1",
          "r2",
          "r3",
